---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="JS Particle Engine — Dylan McCurry">
  <span class="eyebrow">Look what I built, long before AI was a thing</span>
  <h1>JS Particle Engine</h1>
  <p class="muted">
    A WebGL particle system built from scratch for a game engine architecture course at MTSU
    (Middle Tennessee State University) — flames, fog, and a rotating textured cube, all hand-rolled
    shader code. Circa 2011, no framework, no AI, just raw GLSL and jQuery UI sliders.
  </p>
  <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <span class="tag">WebGL</span>
    <span class="tag">GLSL</span>
    <span class="tag">2011</span>
  </div>
  <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/jdylanmc/JS-Particle-Engine" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View on GitHub ↗</a>

  <h2>Live demo</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    Drag the sliders to control force, angle, spawn rate, speed, and lifetime. Pick a texture from
    the dropdown to swap the particle sprite.
  </p>
  <div class="demo-frame">
    <iframe
      src="/demos/particle-engine/index.html"
      title="JS Particle Engine demo"
      loading="lazy"
      width="1024"
      height="768"
    ></iframe>
  </div>

  <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/projects">&larr; Back to projects</a>
</Layout>

<style>
  .demo-frame {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: auto;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .demo-frame iframe {
    display: block;
    border: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
</style>
